deliberately corrupted output, captured to characterise the prefill-trace hazard
This directory holds completions from a server running with prefill traces resident,
captured on purpose while reproducing the failure in doc/optimized_vllm/README.md
(*The bug this stage found*). They are partly or wholly replacement characters.

check_degenerate_output.py skips a directory carrying this marker and REPORTS the
exclusion with this file's first line as the reason, so the artifacts stay under
their real names, stay discoverable and stay readable by a reviewer -- including the
two sets that straddle the threshold (traced_qualitative and soak_blocking/runner_qual1
are clean on prompts 0-3 and corrupt from prompt 4, which is the onset boundary and the
minimal reproducer). Naming a file here explicitly on the command line still scans it,
which is how logs/degenerate_check_negative_control.log is produced.
